{title: The God of Abraham Praise}
{artist: Thomas Olivers}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
The [Em]God of Abraham [Am]praise, who [B]reigns en[Em]throned above —
[G]Ancient of ever[Am]lasting [B]days and [Em]God of [B]love.
Je[Em]hovah, great I [Am]AM, by [B]earth and [Em]heaven confessed,
[G]I bow and bless the [Am]sacred [B]name for[Em]ever [B]blessed.

Verse 2
The [Em]God of Abr'ham praise, [Am]at Whose [B]supreme command From earth I
[G]rise and seek [B]the joys at [Em]His right [B]hand;
I all on [Am]earth forsake, its [B]wisdom, fame, [Em]and pow'r;
[G]And Him my only Portion make, [Am]my [B]Shield and [B]Tow'r.

Verse 3
The [Em]God of Abr'ham praise, [Am]Whose all sufficient [B]grace Shall guide me all
[G]my happy days, [B]in all my [Em]ways. He [B]calls
a worm His [Am]friend, He calls [B]Himself my [Em]God! And
[G]He shall save me to the [Am]end, [B]thro' Jesus' [B]blood.

Verse 4
He [Em]by Himself has [Am]sworn; I on [B]His oath depend, I
[G]shall, on eagle [B]wings upborne, [Em]to Heav'n [B]ascend.
I shall behold [Am]His face; [B]I shall [Em]His pow'r
[G]adore, And sing the wonders [Am]of [B]His grace [B]forevermore.

Verse 5
Tho' [Em]nature's strength decay, [Am]and earth and [B]hell withstand, To Canaan's
[G]bounds I urge [B]my way, [Em]at His [B]command.
The wat'ry deep [Am]I pass, [B]with Jesus [Em]in my
[G]view; And thro' the howling [Am]wilderness [B]my way [B]pursue.
